.\" improv-formulas(7): the formula language, condensed from docs/src/formulas.md.
.TH IMPROV-FORMULAS 7 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv-formulas \- the Improv formula language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I Target
.B =
.I expression
.SH DESCRIPTION
A formula defines a derived measure in terms of other measures and
categories, never cell addresses: the rule is written once and applies to
every cell of the target. Names resolve against the model, so every
measure and category a formula names must exist; the target need not.
.PP
.B improv add-derived
takes the expression only;
.B improv define
takes the whole definition.
.SH OPERATORS
From lowest to highest precedence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
OR                       left-associative
AND                      left-associative
NOT                      prefix; applies to a whole comparison
== <> != < <= > >=       at most one per level: a < b < c is an error
&                        text join
+ \-                      left-associative
* /                      left-associative
\-                        unary minus
^                        power, right-associative: 2^3^2 is 512, \-2^2 is \-4
%                        postfix: x% is x / 100
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B =
is only the assignment after the target; equality is
.BR == .
Keywords and function names are case-insensitive.
.SH VALUES
Numbers
.RB ( 42 ,
.BR 1.07 ;
no exponent, no leading point), text in double quotes
.RB ( \(dqhello\(dq ,
no escapes), booleans
.RB ( TRUE ,
.BR FALSE ),
dates
.RB ( #2025-01-01# )
and date-times
.RB ( #2025-01-01T09:30:00Z# ).
An error is a value:
.BR #DIV/0! ,
.BR #NUM! ,
.BR #VALUE! ,
.BR #N/A .
An operator or function given an error returns it;
.B IFERROR
and
.B ISERROR
handle them. A missing cell is not an error: where an input has no cell,
the result has none.
.SH NAMES
A bare name starts with a letter or
.B _
and continues with letters, digits or
.BR _ .
Any other name goes in single quotes, with
.B \(aq\(aq
for a quote:
.BR "\(aqBob\(aq\(aqs Rate\(aq" .
A quoted name is always a measure or category, never a keyword.
.SH AGGREGATIONS
.nf
Total  = SUM(Revenue OVER Time)
Others = SUM(Revenue OVER ALL EXCEPT Product)
Big    = SUM(Revenue OVER Time WHERE Revenue > 1000)
Rank   = RANK(Revenue OVER Product)
.fi
.PP
.IB F ( Measure " OVER " Categories )
collapses those categories.
.B WHERE
keeps the cells where its condition holds. The reduced arguments are
measure references; rows reach the reduction in item order.
.IB Measure [ Cat ", ...]"
keeps only the listed categories.
.SH POSITIONS AND RECURRENCES
.nf
Growth  = Revenue \- PREV(Revenue, Time, 1, 0)
Running = SUM(Revenue OVER Time[FIRST..THIS])
Balance = PREV(Balance, Time, 1, Opening) + Deposits
.fi
.PP
.BR POSITION ,
.BR @ITEM ,
.BR PREV ,
.B NEXT
and windows
.BI OVER " T" [ from .. to ]
use a category's item order. A measure may read its own earlier values
through
.BR PREV ;
any other cycle between measures is an error, and
.B improv define
refuses it.
.SH LET, LAMBDA AND LISTS
.nf
Margin = LET(rev, Price * Quantity, (rev \- Cost) / rev)
Final  = REDUCE(0, Deposits OVER Time, LAMBDA(acc, d, acc * 1.01 + d))
Top    = SORT(Sales OVER Product, \-1 INTO Rank)
.fi
.PP
.BR LET ,
.BR LAMBDA ,
.BR MAP ,
.BR SCAN ,
.B REDUCE
and
.B MAKEARRAY
are supported. A named LAMBDA
.RB ( "improv define m.db 1 \(dqMargin = LAMBDA(p, c, p \- c)\(dq" )
is called by name. A list result says where it lands:
.B INTO
a category.
.B FIXPOINT(init, LAMBDA(r, step), [max_iter], [tolerance])
iterates to a fixed point and always terminates.
.SH SOURCE FORMS
Only as a whole right-hand side, through
.BR "improv define" :
.B CALL(fn, m1, ...)
(an external function, populated by
.BR "improv refresh-ext" )
and
.B SQL(\(dqquery\(dq)
(use
.BR "improv import-sql" ).
.SH LOCALE
.B improv define
and
.B add-derived
read formulas in the locale named by
.BR IMPROV_LOCALE ,
else the OS locale. In German a formula uses German function names, a
decimal comma and
.B ;
between arguments:
.BR "WENN(Price > 1,5; RUNDEN(Price; 2); 0)" .
The English spelling is always accepted; models store it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-functions (7),
.BR improv-files (5).
The full language: docs/src/formulas.md, or The Formula Language in the
user guide, https://gregburd.codeberg.page/improv/.
